<title>TUNISIA: EIB to lend Tunisia 40 million ECUs.</title>
<headline>EIB to lend Tunisia 40 million ECUs.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Investment Bank has granted Tunisia two loans totalling 40 million ECUs ($46 million) to finance private sector firms and work on a railway, the European Commission said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said the first loan of 15 million European Currency Units was to help boost the capital of private firms trying to modernise and restructure themselves.</p>
<p>The second loan of 25 million ECUs was to finance work on the Tunis-Sfax-Gabes railway linking the northern and southern regions of the country.</p>
</text>
